WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.825 --> 01:30.745
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.664 --> 01:33.999
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.875 --> 01:35.918
Black Jack.

01:49.270 --> 01:59.444
Whiteair Flight 203 from New York
has just arrived at Gate 36.

02:05.688 --> 02:07.166
Is it done already?

02:07.750 --> 02:10.878
I'm so busy.

02:12.964 --> 02:16.008
Who would be so rude as to call when I'm so busy?!

02:16.009 --> 02:16.508
Yes.

02:16.527 --> 02:17.759
Yes. Yes. Yes. Yes.

02:19.220 --> 02:20.679
Oh, Doc!

02:21.057 --> 02:21.850
Pinoco?

02:22.020 --> 02:23.640
Yeah, I'm at the airport.

02:23.683 --> 02:25.100
I'm about to head home.

02:25.322 --> 02:27.464
Doc, did you get me a souvenir?

02:27.465 --> 02:29.883
Did you get the chocolate I wanted from America?

02:29.884 --> 02:31.176
Yeah, I did.

02:31.302 --> 02:32.933
That makes me happy!

02:33.550 --> 02:38.475
Also, someone called wanting to schedule a checkup.

02:38.751 --> 02:40.352
Let me get home first.

02:40.353 --> 02:41.686
Right.

02:41.870 --> 02:43.563
I'm sure you're exhausted,

02:43.564 --> 02:46.144
so I'll prepare the bath and a meal for you.

02:46.589 --> 02:48.204
I'm not exhausted.

02:48.601 --> 02:51.279
You're working too hard.

02:51.280 --> 02:54.783
You've been away in America for
a whole week, so you need to...

02:54.961 --> 02:55.700
That's it!

02:55.701 --> 02:59.913
You need to relax with me in front of the TV!

02:59.914 --> 03:01.636
Don't be silly, Pinoco.

03:01.791 --> 03:02.618
I'll see you soon.

03:03.793 --> 03:05.669
Oh yeah, the pot...

03:07.303 --> 03:08.463
Is it Doc again?

03:08.840 --> 03:09.500
Yes?

03:11.103 --> 03:12.103
It's not?

03:12.301 --> 03:13.510
You're a patient?

03:15.283 --> 03:18.363
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "The Cholera Epidemic"

03:15.283 --> 03:18.363
The Cholera Epidemic

03:20.143 --> 03:22.699
Hey, Black Jack!

03:24.076 --> 03:25.788
Long time no see!

03:26.065 --> 03:27.440
Is that you, Andoh?

03:27.441 --> 03:30.152
I haven't seen you since our class reunion two years ago.

03:30.153 --> 03:31.736
Where'd you fly in from?

03:31.737 --> 03:33.613
From the US.

03:33.810 --> 03:35.365
I see.

03:35.499 --> 03:37.117
I was just in Southeast Asia.

03:37.118 --> 03:39.411
It was the usual thing I do with
the Japan Medical Association.

03:39.412 --> 03:41.246
Let's go out for a quick drink,

03:41.247 --> 03:42.372
and catch up a bit.

03:43.207 --> 03:45.959
But aren't they waiting for you?

03:45.960 --> 03:50.277
After staying with them for five days
and nights, I'm tired of them.

03:50.464 --> 03:52.260
Come on. Don't be a stranger.

03:52.592 --> 03:54.801
Sorry, but I'm exhausted.

03:54.869 --> 03:57.888
Oh, come on! We're old classmates, aren't we?

04:01.058 --> 04:03.602
Gosh, did I miss Japanese food.

04:05.139 --> 04:07.105
This is really good too!

04:07.106 --> 04:08.982
Come on. Eat!

04:08.983 --> 04:11.860
The food over there was good, but it was so hot.

04:11.861 --> 04:13.653
It really got to me.

04:15.781 --> 04:17.417
Did you undergo quarantine?

04:17.575 --> 04:19.367
It's not like I'm sick or anything,

04:19.368 --> 04:20.952
so I didn't bother.

04:21.454 --> 04:23.580
Are you sure you're OK?

04:23.581 --> 04:26.124
You're too cautious.

04:26.488 --> 04:29.961
Doctors are supposed to be cautious about these things.

04:31.380 --> 04:34.007
That doesn't sound like something an
underground doctor should say.

04:36.130 --> 04:39.721
So, I hear you're making good money.

04:40.931 --> 04:43.808
Exactly how much?

04:44.644 --> 04:45.810
Who knows?

04:46.771 --> 04:50.231
You're so twisted.

04:51.984 --> 04:53.777
Excuse me for a moment.

05:02.912 --> 05:03.765
What's wrong?

05:04.232 --> 05:05.473
Strange...

05:05.864 --> 05:07.707
No, it's nothing.

05:09.627 --> 05:11.378
I'm going to head home now.

05:11.921 --> 05:13.713
What's the rush?

05:14.840 --> 05:17.471
Shouldn't you go home soon too?

05:18.344 --> 05:20.052
Right...

05:27.097 --> 05:29.307
Um, I have to...

05:29.308 --> 05:30.889
Later!

05:35.090 --> 05:36.440
What the...

05:38.905 --> 05:40.640
And now the news.

05:40.861 --> 05:46.741
Numerous doctors who were on Blueriver
Airlines flight 607 from Southeast Asia

05:46.742 --> 05:49.243
have been diagnosed with cholera.

05:49.244 --> 05:51.579
This group was comprised of thirty-eight doctors.

05:51.580 --> 05:54.916
The number of those confirmed to
have been infected is now up to...

06:00.631 --> 06:03.466
<i>Damn. I might have been infected!</i>

06:04.278 --> 06:07.178
Hey, I'm sorry, but can we change the destination?

06:11.223 --> 06:12.350
It must be Doc!

06:13.268 --> 06:16.521
Doc! Welcome home!

06:20.818 --> 06:23.596
So, this is Dr. Black Jack's clinic?

06:23.904 --> 06:25.196
It's small.

06:25.445 --> 06:27.490
Who are you?

06:27.491 --> 06:31.702
I called earlier about the doctor giving me a checkup?

06:31.703 --> 06:34.163
He's not home yet.

06:35.243 --> 06:36.624
He's coming back soon, right?

06:36.625 --> 06:38.042
I'll wait until then.

06:38.043 --> 06:41.671
He'll be tired, so he won't be seeing anyone.

06:42.589 --> 06:45.675
He's the one who'll decide that.

06:45.676 --> 06:48.886
That's not something you should decide!

06:48.887 --> 06:50.346
Go home!

06:50.513 --> 06:52.598
Who are you anyway?

06:52.698 --> 06:54.058
The doctor's kid?

06:54.146 --> 06:56.686
I'm his wife.

06:58.392 --> 07:01.732
I don't care, as long as he can treat me.

07:02.216 --> 07:05.570
I hear he asks for a crazy amount of money though.

07:06.238 --> 07:09.031
But it doesn't look like he's making that much.

07:09.283 --> 07:12.410
Hey! That's Doc's seat!

07:15.119 --> 07:16.439
What's wrong?

07:16.942 --> 07:19.208
The usual dizziness...

07:21.286 --> 07:23.588
Oh no!

07:25.465 --> 07:26.173
Thanks.

07:26.174 --> 07:27.425
Keep the change.

07:45.857 --> 07:48.195
<i>It might be too late for the vaccination to work.</i>

07:57.763 --> 08:00.124
Doc, where are you?

08:00.250 --> 08:02.918
Something came up, so l can't come home tonight.

08:04.106 --> 08:05.671
You can't?

08:05.746 --> 08:06.706
No, I can't.

08:07.140 --> 08:09.508
I can't for at least a few days.

08:09.509 --> 08:11.719
That's too mean!

08:11.720 --> 08:15.556
I've been waiting for you with the bath all prepared.

08:15.557 --> 08:18.726
Also, a patient is in trouble.

08:18.727 --> 08:19.477
A patient?

08:20.062 --> 08:22.188
She fell unconscious all of a sudden.

08:22.457 --> 08:23.690
What's going. on?

08:23.780 --> 08:28.152
She just barged in after I told her you'd be home soon.

08:28.951 --> 08:29.737
What?

08:29.738 --> 08:30.946
She has a fever?

08:31.141 --> 08:32.323
And her pulse?

08:32.324 --> 08:33.365
Does she have a pulse?

08:34.526 --> 08:36.044
There's no pulse?

08:36.323 --> 08:37.495
What about her blood pressure?

08:37.496 --> 08:38.454
Did you check it?

08:38.455 --> 08:40.539
Blood pressure...

08:43.417 --> 08:45.073
150/100?

08:45.601 --> 08:47.254
That's quite high.

08:48.563 --> 08:49.382
What?!

08:49.383 --> 08:50.591
Of course.

08:50.592 --> 08:53.302
It should be the same on both arms.

08:53.303 --> 08:54.804
You must have mismeasured it.

08:54.994 --> 08:57.015
Doc, please come home.

08:57.490 --> 09:00.518
I can't handle this by myself.

09:00.787 --> 09:03.020
Hush! Don't be so negative!

09:03.259 --> 09:05.231
You're my assistant!

09:06.331 --> 09:07.858
Ensure that the patient lies still.

09:07.987 --> 09:09.318
It's better not to do anything rash.

09:09.523 --> 09:11.195
And make sure she lays on her side.

09:11.196 --> 09:12.905
Yeah.

09:16.243 --> 09:18.869
I can't do it!

09:18.922 --> 09:20.906
I can't come home for a few days.

09:21.123 --> 09:23.082
Take care of the patient until then.

09:23.452 --> 09:25.292
It may be pulse less disease.

09:25.293 --> 09:27.670
Call for an ambulance immediately if
something goes drastically wrong.

09:29.464 --> 09:31.132
Doc, that's so mean!

09:31.293 --> 09:34.344
Sheesh, what's all that noise about?
Doc, that's so mean!

09:35.408 --> 09:37.012
Where's the medical ward?

09:37.140 --> 09:38.305
The medical ward?

09:38.445 --> 09:40.474
I'm a patient.

09:40.475 --> 09:42.143
I'll be staying here.

09:43.645 --> 09:47.690
I'm not allergic to any kind of food,
so just bring something soon.

09:50.776 --> 09:52.820
Ohmigewdness!

09:54.672 --> 09:55.865
Right.

09:56.140 --> 09:59.285
About that cholera epidemic.

09:59.286 --> 10:02.329
Can you check into what happened to Andoh?

10:02.686 --> 10:05.791
Andoh? You mean our former classmate?

10:06.117 --> 10:06.792
Yeah.

10:06.793 --> 10:09.420
I might have caught cholera from him.

10:10.255 --> 10:11.463
Now?

10:11.464 --> 10:12.797
Yes, I'm alone.

10:13.268 --> 10:17.261
It's the office in the small clinic I used
to use when I first started practicing.

10:18.137 --> 10:24.463
I have quite an array of patients, so I've
kept this place just as it was back then.

10:25.100 --> 10:27.982
I never dreamed I'd be using it like this though.

10:28.148 --> 10:31.108
Do you have any antibiotics in case it develops?

10:31.301 --> 10:32.026
No.

10:32.375 --> 10:34.446
I'll ask you for them if it happens.

10:34.669 --> 10:36.947
Anyway, let me know about Andoh.

10:36.948 --> 10:38.490
Sure.

10:47.850 --> 10:49.126
It's me.

10:49.127 --> 10:50.628
He was infected.

10:50.963 --> 10:53.798
He's been hospitalized along with the other doctors.

10:53.955 --> 10:55.148
I knew it.

10:59.780 --> 11:02.932
The number of those known to be infected
with cholera has increased by six,

11:02.933 --> 11:04.558
making the total number now thirty-four...

11:04.915 --> 11:11.148
Staff at the emergency center are worried that those who
had contact with the doctors may also be infected.

11:11.730 --> 11:14.308
<i>There isn't any evidence of the presence
of cholera bacteria for now.</i>

11:14.944 --> 11:17.363
<i>If I am infected, signs should show
up either today or tomorrow.</i>

11:31.008 --> 11:32.836
You're not a good cook, are you?

11:33.502 --> 11:36.796
If you don't like it, go somewhere else.

11:36.797 --> 11:42.010
I've seen many doctors, but there weren't any good ones.

11:42.241 --> 11:46.307
Dr. Black Jack can treat anything, right?

11:46.473 --> 11:49.350
Or is he just a quack and can't really do jack?

11:49.560 --> 11:51.811
He's not a quack!

11:52.117 --> 11:57.150
But, perhaps, not even Dr. Black Jack can treat me.

11:57.307 --> 11:59.606
Yes, he can!

12:00.151 --> 12:04.324
Then I have to see him.

12:04.325 --> 12:07.054
But he's not coming home yet.

12:07.203 --> 12:09.621
We don't even know where he is.

12:11.617 --> 12:12.791
That must be Doc!

12:14.710 --> 12:17.212
Doc, where are you?

12:17.213 --> 12:18.171
Tell me!

12:18.477 --> 12:21.216
Why can't you tell me?-

12:21.217 --> 12:22.342
Doc, you dummy!

12:22.649 --> 12:23.887
Dummy!

12:23.969 --> 12:26.596
You're with a girl, aren't.you?!

12:26.990 --> 12:29.468
Pinoco, listen carefully.

12:29.619 --> 12:32.470
I may be infected with a contagious disease.

12:32.756 --> 12:37.225
So if I operate on a patient now
I'll infect the patient as well.

12:37.346 --> 12:38.184
Understand?

12:38.185 --> 12:41.146
Just come home soon, Doc!

12:41.382 --> 12:46.152
If I'm really infected, the incubation period
should end either today or tomorrow.

12:46.152 --> 12:51.114
So I'll come home after then if nothing happens.

12:51.115 --> 12:53.533
Well, then tell me where you are.

12:53.534 --> 12:55.327
I'll come right there.

12:55.636 --> 12:57.579
I knew you'd say that.

12:57.788 --> 12:59.915
That's why there's no way I can tell you.

13:01.709 --> 13:04.586
Just wait patiently for a day or two.

13:04.587 --> 13:07.047
In any case, call for an ambulance and
transfer the patient somewhere else.

13:07.048 --> 13:07.631
OK?

13:07.689 --> 13:09.174
But Doc!

13:09.313 --> 13:09.924
OK?

13:10.105 --> 13:11.092
Thanks!

13:14.943 --> 13:18.725
Pinoco must be throwing a fit by now.

13:27.128 --> 13:28.995
Oh, Pinoco-chan.

13:29.152 --> 13:32.707
Huh?! You want me to help you find Doc?!

13:32.708 --> 13:35.794
It's Sunday today so you‘re free right?

13:35.996 --> 13:40.340
Actually, I have a lot of homework to do.

13:40.341 --> 13:42.945
It's your fault for letting it all pile up.

13:43.344 --> 13:45.804
You're not leaving until you finish all off it.

13:45.805 --> 13:47.431
So just as you heard,

13:47.432 --> 13:48.014
bye.

13:49.642 --> 13:51.226
Sharaku, you dummy!

13:51.227 --> 13:51.852
Dummy!

13:51.853 --> 13:53.186
Dummy!

13:55.690 --> 13:57.741
Hello, is this a private detective?

13:57.794 --> 14:00.360
I need you to find Doc.

14:00.800 --> 14:03.488
I don't like prank calls, Missy!

14:05.199 --> 14:09.661
Don't treat me like a kid!

14:10.413 --> 14:13.035
Largo, go find Doc.

14:13.291 --> 14:16.293
Now, take me to Doc.

14:20.715 --> 14:25.260
Even Largo's mocking me!

14:28.890 --> 14:30.182
What's going on?

14:30.183 --> 14:33.935
These are the love letters I was going
to send Doc while he was away!

14:34.433 --> 14:35.086
Geez!

14:35.159 --> 14:37.464
I hate them! I hate them! I hate them!

14:37.465 --> 14:38.924
You're such a crybaby.

14:38.925 --> 14:41.260
Sorry I'm crybaby!

14:41.261 --> 14:44.888
Quit whining and go somewhere else!

14:45.210 --> 14:49.644
The number of those infected with cholera
is now up to sixty-eight and counting.

14:49.882 --> 14:51.979
The emergency center has now...

14:56.159 --> 14:58.777
If it's going to break out, it'll be soon.

15:03.609 --> 15:07.828
When that happens, I'll be extremely dehydrated
and have an acute pain in my stomach.

15:09.360 --> 15:11.957
I wonder what Pinoco's up to.

15:25.388 --> 15:27.124
Doc...

15:39.319 --> 15:40.527
Does it hurt?

15:40.671 --> 15:42.279
I don't know what to do...

15:43.615 --> 15:44.531
She has a fever,

15:44.532 --> 15:45.329
her hands feel weak,

15:45.329 --> 15:46.116
she gets tired easily,

15:46.117 --> 15:47.159
she often feels dizzy,

15:47.160 --> 15:48.619
she occasionally falls unconscious,

15:48.620 --> 15:49.786
she has high blood pressure,

15:49.787 --> 15:50.996
and no pulse.

15:50.997 --> 15:53.498
What should I do when all that happens?!

15:53.670 --> 15:55.584
l can't breathe...

15:56.169 --> 15:58.420
Here. I brought something to lower your fever.

15:58.622 --> 16:00.882
It'll bring your fever down, so take it.

16:01.424 --> 16:02.768
I can't...

16:03.092 --> 16:04.618
I can't see.

16:04.685 --> 16:05.927
It's dark.

16:07.571 --> 16:08.806
Where are you?

16:08.938 --> 16:10.328
Where's the medicine?

16:10.683 --> 16:12.351
I can't see.

16:12.352 --> 16:14.227
What should we do?!

16:14.406 --> 16:15.187
Hang on.

16:15.188 --> 16:16.938
I'll go look it up!

16:17.815 --> 16:22.444
Let's see... an illness that causes blindness...?

16:22.747 --> 16:24.363
I can't move my arms!

16:24.364 --> 16:27.949
Please don't have so many things going wrong at once!

16:28.868 --> 16:31.828
I'll make medicine for you.

16:38.005 --> 16:39.336
Hang in there!

16:39.337 --> 16:41.505
I'm making medicine right now!

16:46.552 --> 16:48.095
Somebody...

16:49.931 --> 16:51.014
What's wrong?

16:51.015 --> 16:52.140
Are you OK?

16:53.518 --> 16:54.476
Come on!

16:54.477 --> 16:57.354
Did you fall unconscious again?

16:58.731 --> 17:00.565
Her pupils are dilated.

17:00.566 --> 17:03.735
I can't hear a heartbeat.

17:05.010 --> 17:06.738
She's not breathing.

17:07.365 --> 17:09.408
Did she die?!

17:09.409 --> 17:11.097
Please don't die!

17:14.580 --> 17:16.576
I'm sorry!

17:27.013 --> 17:28.009
Doc...

17:28.723 --> 17:30.137
It's too late.

17:31.806 --> 17:32.264
Dummy!

17:32.348 --> 17:32.681
Dummy!

17:32.776 --> 17:33.117
Dummy!

17:33.141 --> 17:33.640
Dummy!

17:33.641 --> 17:35.976
Where have you been all this time?!

17:36.101 --> 17:38.103
She's already dead!

17:45.403 --> 17:48.488
Why didn't you transfer the patient somewhere else?!

17:48.489 --> 17:51.449
She refused to go anywhere else.

17:52.226 --> 17:53.742
She's not dead yet.

17:54.162 --> 17:55.912
But she is in a coma.

17:56.074 --> 17:57.789
She's not dead?

17:57.931 --> 18:00.042
Pinoco, prepare to operate.

18:03.296 --> 18:04.379
Preparing to operate.

18:04.569 --> 18:05.547
Preparing to operate.

18:05.548 --> 18:06.423
So busy.

18:06.465 --> 18:07.841
So busy.

18:08.520 --> 18:10.316
Give the patient vasculat.

18:11.723 --> 18:13.310
Aye-aye!

18:14.977 --> 18:16.349
Vasculat...

18:16.350 --> 18:18.727
Pinoco, can I have something to drink?

18:18.836 --> 18:20.453
To drink?

18:20.771 --> 18:21.354
Beverage...

18:21.397 --> 18:22.379
Beverage...

18:24.692 --> 18:27.499
Here you go, Doc.

18:31.824 --> 18:32.638
All right.

18:37.830 --> 18:40.081
If she has a stroke, it'll be too late to do anything.

18:40.245 --> 18:41.875
One of her carotid arteries has occluded.

18:42.896 --> 18:43.585
Scalpel.

18:43.953 --> 18:44.837
Here.

18:59.671 --> 19:00.808
Vascular graft.

19:02.022 --> 19:03.369
Atraumatic needle.

19:04.377 --> 19:05.473
Vascular clamp.

19:10.686 --> 19:11.613
OK.

19:11.720 --> 19:14.950
Her cerebral blood circulation should temporarily improve.

19:15.115 --> 19:16.409
Is it done?

19:16.653 --> 19:18.536
We've saved her life for now.

19:18.537 --> 19:19.663
That's all we can do today.

19:19.896 --> 19:21.665
We'll replace the bad artery in her abdomen tomorrow.

19:22.249 --> 19:23.708
I see.

19:27.948 --> 19:30.090
Doc, you were so mean.

19:30.091 --> 19:32.133
I was so worried.

19:32.532 --> 19:35.173
l put myself under quarantine.

19:35.759 --> 19:38.501
I was afraid I might be infected with cholera.

19:39.308 --> 19:40.725
Cholera?

19:41.352 --> 19:43.220
Didn't you hear about it on the news?

19:43.620 --> 19:47.399
Cholera breaks out two or three
days after an infection occurs.

19:47.558 --> 19:49.791
That's why I couldn't come home.

19:51.070 --> 19:53.113
Are you fine now?

19:53.589 --> 19:56.800
After three days, I didn't have either
diarrhea or pains in my stomach.

19:57.118 --> 19:59.369
I should be fine.

20:02.355 --> 20:04.059
I feel kind of strange.

20:04.333 --> 20:06.084
What's wrong, Doc?

20:06.085 --> 20:07.711
Something feels odd.

20:10.464 --> 20:11.756
No!

20:11.986 --> 20:13.049
Could it be...

20:13.818 --> 20:15.680
What do you mean?

20:29.981 --> 20:32.453
So I was infected with cholera after all?

20:33.696 --> 20:34.725
Damn!

20:35.114 --> 20:36.156
Why now?!

20:36.285 --> 20:37.907
You have cholera?!

20:38.268 --> 20:41.161
Pinoco, we must put this house under total isolation.

20:41.162 --> 20:43.044
Don't go outside no matter what.

20:43.414 --> 20:45.081
Also, that patient...

20:45.666 --> 20:48.084
She is probably infected too.

20:48.461 --> 20:50.462
The operation was a failure!

20:50.463 --> 20:53.381
It's my fault.

20:54.414 --> 20:58.178
Doc, isn't there anything we can do?

20:58.704 --> 21:00.346
We need antibiotics.

21:00.347 --> 21:04.001
I'll call him and ask him to send them immediately.

21:04.185 --> 21:08.271
Hang on. I can make the medicine.

21:08.772 --> 21:11.313
No, don't get any funny ideas.

21:11.834 --> 21:13.193
Why?

21:13.294 --> 21:16.571
I'm good at making medicine.

21:19.572 --> 21:20.177
Oh?

21:20.201 --> 21:22.160
Where's the medicine I left here?

21:23.259 --> 21:24.121
Medicine?!

21:26.081 --> 21:31.085
I gave him the medicine I made for the patient!

21:32.584 --> 21:34.297
You mean that juice earlier?!

21:34.459 --> 21:35.298
Yeah.

21:35.299 --> 21:36.299
It had a drug to lower a fever,

21:36.300 --> 21:36.925
a pain-killer,

21:36.926 --> 21:38.009
a stimulant,

21:38.010 --> 21:39.177
anti-itching powder,

21:39.178 --> 21:43.056
and hemorrhoid medicine all mixed together.

21:40.037 --> 21:41.857
That's why...

21:43.455 --> 21:46.018
Ohmigewdness.

21:46.463 --> 21:49.896
Doc, would you like rice porridge for dinner?

21:49.897 --> 21:52.273
Or maybe you should stay on the safe
side and just have the leftover broth?

21:53.943 --> 21:58.289
Or would you like one of Pinoco's
special medical concoctions?

21:58.782 --> 22:01.407
Never ever make that again!

22:01.454 --> 22:04.928
But aren't you glad that it wasn't cholera?

22:07.087 --> 22:19.042
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.087 --> 22:19.042
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.160 --> 22:24.159
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.160 --> 22:24.159
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.728 --> 22:31.197
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.728 --> 22:31.197
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.741 --> 22:37.199
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.741 --> 22:37.199
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.803 --> 22:40.288
being heated up by you,

22:37.803 --> 22:40.288
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.497 --> 22:48.274
so much that I change color

22:40.497 --> 22:48.274
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.359 --> 23:00.128
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.359 --> 23:00.128
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.336 --> 23:12.067
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.336 --> 23:12.067
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.307 --> 23:23.658
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.307 --> 23:23.658
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.844 --> 23:28.765
I couldn't be happier

23:23.844 --> 23:28.765
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:28.993 --> 23:33.927
How does it taste?

23:28.993 --> 23:33.926
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.083 --> 24:15.072
The Abacus Prodigy

23:47.670 --> 23:48.670
What's that?

23:49.024 --> 23:50.024
This?

23:51.601 --> 23:52.308
Reiji-kun!

23:52.367 --> 23:54.047
The abacus wasn't for me.

23:54.156 --> 23:56.495
If they laugh at you, laugh back at them.

23:56.567 --> 23:59.408
He will be depressed if he can't use the abacus,
which he loves so much, again.

23:59.542 --> 24:01.158
You're trying to be the best?

24:01.482 --> 24:03.957
The sound of an abacus is like my dad's voice.

24:04.407 --> 24:08.158
Please calculate seven-million, five-hundred
fifty-seven thousand...

24:08.159 --> 24:09.397
Keep going.

24:10.078 --> 24:11.497
My finger...

24:11.950 --> 24:14.746
Next Karte - The Abacus Prodigy.

24:15.385 --> 24:17.292
Karte NG...

24:18.845 --> 24:20.045
It must be Doc!

24:22.478 --> 24:24.640
Doc where are you?
